  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 232 AM CDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\nThe first chance of rain makes an appearance later this weekend\nas the remnants of Hurricane Isaias move into the area. The low\npressure system is forecast to move north through eastern LA/AR\nand could clip the eastern Ozarks Saturday night into Sunday. \nIt won't bring widespread rainfall, and areas west of highway 63\nwill likely stay dry. Right now we have a 30-50% chance of rain\nfor the eastern Ozarks for Saturday night with rain dissipating\nby Sunday morning. The track of the system will determine where\nthe rain will fall. Though, models are mostly in agreement that\nthe building ridge over the Central Plains this weekend will \nkeep the remnants east and push it towards the Ohio River \nValley. This means it'll be more likely for the system to go \nfurther east than shift back towards the west. For this reason,\nwe have kept POPs around 50% or less.\n\nHighs through the weekend and into the start of next week will \nsit in the mid 80s once again as the high pressure continues to \nbuild and stay put over the Central Plains into the start of \nnext week. Though, looking into the end of next week, we could\nsee a pattern change a week from today. There are still model\ndiscrepancies, but perhaps fall makes an appearance once again.",
